          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mt2m771b6pxbgwk4",
          "message": {
            "text": "Hiding stale notes is a simple .filter(n => !n.stale) because staleness is ALREADY relative to what's being reviewed — the maintainer's 'show it at an older commit' nuance falls out for free.\n\nreanchorReviewNotes(notes, finalDiff) flags a note stale by matching its authored snippet against finalDiff's content. For a --commit <sha> (or range) review, finalDiff is THAT commit's diff, so a note whose code still matches at that commit is NOT flagged stale → it renders as valid context 'as of the commit time'. At HEAD, where the code moved on, the same note IS flagged → hidden. So one unconditional filter satisfies both 'no need to show outdated notes' and 'but show them when reviewing an older commit before the change'. No commit-time comparison logic was needed. The context-reveal path (GB-1139) already filters the same way; the GB-907 outdated-badge + Keep/Discard UI was removed.",
            "markdown": "Hiding stale notes is a simple `.filter(n => !n.stale)` because staleness is ALREADY relative to what's being reviewed — the maintainer's 'show it at an older commit' nuance falls out for free.\n\n`reanchorReviewNotes(notes, finalDiff)` flags a note stale by matching its authored snippet against `finalDiff`'s content. For a `--commit <sha>` (or range) review, finalDiff is THAT commit's diff, so a note whose code still matches at that commit is NOT flagged stale → it renders as valid context 'as of the commit time'. At HEAD, where the code moved on, the same note IS flagged → hidden. So one unconditional filter satisfies both 'no need to show outdated notes' and 'but show them when reviewing an older commit before the change'. No commit-time comparison logic was needed. The context-reveal path (GB-1139) already filters the same way; the GB-907 outdated-badge + Keep/Discard UI was removed."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/routes/pages.tsx"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 173,
                  "endLine": 173,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    : loadReviewNotesForFile(c.get('repoRoot'), file.file_path);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
